<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Spoilers&nbsp;on&nbsp;spoilers</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Put&nbsp;it&nbsp;back&nbsp;in&nbsp;the&nbsp;failsafe&nbsp;Keter&nbsp;safe&nbsp;Safe&nbsp;safe</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>I wonder then, if the Foundation is truly convinced it won't work</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I think it's more of a Hail Mary. Maybe the nukes will kill the satellites and the nanomachine payloads. If we are really lucky, <em>just maybe</em> they'll miss the Earth with their impactor. Worth a shot. I also wanted to imply a bit of an Apollyon here, if we have <em>a plan</em> at least we won't be freaking out about not having a plan. Right?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>the Keter skips that are to be &quot;unsealed&quot; are just to get things over with as quickly as possible,</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Actually my thought was that these are all destruction, neutralization, or K-class mitigation orders (depending on how possible each option is). If the aliens are pulling the trigger that probably means some Keter class object is causing, or is about to cause, some interstellar level K-class trouble might as well shutdown all our Keters and see if the aliens calm down.</p>
</div>
